  <title>
    <media type="image" width="40px" height="40px" its:translate="no" src="figures/orca-logo.svg" /> Notifications
  </title>
  <p>
    Notifications are brief messages from applications or the desktop, such as new-message
    alerts or low-battery warnings. Orca keeps recent notifications it receives so you can
    review an announcement you missed or interrupted. This history is cleared when Orca
    restarts.
  </p>
  <section id="commands-notifications">
    <title>Commands</title>
    <p>
      <em style="strong">Preferences location:</em>
      <gui>Commands</gui> category, <gui>Commands</gui> section, <gui>Notification presenter</gui> group.
    </p>
    <list>
      <item>
        <p>
          <gui>Present last notification message</gui>: Unbound by
          default.
        </p>
        <p>
          Presents the most recent message and how long ago it was received.
        </p>
      </item>
      <item>
        <p>
          <gui>Present previous notification message</gui>: Unbound by
          default.
        </p>
        <p>
          Presents the previous message and how long ago it was received.
        </p>
      </item>
      <item>
        <p>
          <gui>Present next notification message</gui>: Unbound by
          default.
        </p>
        <p>
          Presents the next message and how long ago it was received.
        </p>
      </item>
      <item>
        <p>
          <gui>Present notification messages list</gui>: Unbound by
          default.
        </p>
        <p>
          Opens a list of recent messages, newest first, alongside how long ago each was
          received. Use <key>Up Arrow</key> and <key>Down Arrow</key> to move through the
          messages. Use "Clear" to remove the notification history and close the list. Use
          "Close" to dismiss the list without clearing it.
        </p>
